{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 89, :comments ["<b>And when Moses went in.</b> Two verses that contradict each other — a third comes and decides between them. One verse says, ״וַיְדַבֵּר יהוה אֵלָיו מֵאֹהֶל מוֹעֵד״ (Leviticus 1) — and that is outside the curtain — and one verse says, ״וְדִבַּרְתִּי אִתְּךָ מֵעַל הַכַּפֹּרֶת״ (Exodus 25). This one comes and decides between them: Moses goes into the Tent of Meeting, and there hears the voice coming from above the cover from between the two cherubim — the voice goes out from the heaven to between the two cherubim, and from there goes out to the Tent of Meeting (Sifrei)." "<b>And he heard the voice.</b> One might think a low voice — Scripture says, ״אֶת הַקּוֹל״ — that is the voice that spoke with him at Sinai, and when it reached the entrance it would cease and not go out outside the tent." "<b>Speaking.</b> Like מִתְדַבֵּר — it is the glory of above to say thus: speaking to Himself, and Moses hears from Him." "<b>And He spoke to him.</b> To exclude Aaron from the דִּבְּרוֹת (cf. Sifrei)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:56.541565237Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}